        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "4b71c037-2535-5e30-bd42-602f3ef6cf9c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Castres, Languedoc, France\n- Buildings: Castres Cathedral, Saint Benoît church\n- People: Benedict of Nursia\n- Roles: Christian saint, patron saint of Europe\n- Organizations: Eastern Orthodox Churches, Catholic Church, Oriental Orthodox Churches, Anglican Communion, Old Catholic Churches\n\nFacts:\n- Benedict of Nursia lived from 2 March 480 to 543 or 547 AD.\n- Benedict of Nursia is a Christian saint venerated in the Eastern Orthodox Churches, the Catholic Church, the Oriental Orthodox Churches, the Anglican Communion, and the Old Catholic Churches.\n- Benedict of Nursia is a patron saint of Europe.\n- Castres Cathedral, also called Cathédrale Saint-Benoît de Castres, is now the Roman Catholic church of Saint Benoît, meaning Saint Benedict.\n- Castres Cathedral is a historical religious building in Castres, Languedoc, France.",
